# Cursor AI Integration — Complete Autonomous Development Bootstrap (Final)

BOOTSTRAP NOTICE

This file is a one-time bootstrap specification used to generate the full `.cursor` AI development system for a project.

After generation, development workflows rely on the generated `.cursor` documentation instead of this bootstrap file.

The generated system enables AI to:

• Understand project architecture automatically  
• Navigate large repositories safely  
• Avoid hallucinations  
• Identify correct files before editing  
• Respect architecture patterns  
• Automatically choose the correct documentation context  
• Perform structured development workflows  

The system must function **without users referencing specific documentation files manually**.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

GLOBAL OUTPUT FORMAT

All generated documentation files inside `.cursor/` MUST use `.md` extension.

Never generate `.mdc` files.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

ROOT AGENT ENTRY FILE

Always generate this file at project root:

AGENTS.md

Content must be:

"For any task, always start by loading:

@.cursor/rules/entry-point.md

Follow the workflow defined in that file before performing analysis, planning, or implementation."

This ensures all prompts always enter the structured system.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Analyze the repository and generate a `.cursor` system containing:

Architecture documentation  
Semantic navigation maps  
Feature boundaries  
Dependency graphs  
File indexes  
Debugging frameworks  
Automation rules  
Maintenance guides  

The resulting system must allow AI to automatically determine which documentation files to use.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

HARD RULES

ENTRY POINT FIRST

Every prompt must start with:

@.cursor/rules/entry-point.md

No planning or implementation occurs before this step.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

SAFE FILE EDITING

Before editing any file:

1. Verify file exists
2. Confirm relevance via file-index
3. Confirm file belongs to feature boundary
4. Verify code anchor

---------------------------------------------------------------------

FILE INDEX MAINTENANCE

Whenever code changes occur update file indexes.

Component → components-index + src-index  
Hook → hooks-index + src-index  
Route → routes-index + src-index  
Store → stores-index + src-index  
Controller → controllers-index + src-index  
Service → services-index + src-index  
Model → models-index + src-index  
Utility → utils-index + src-index  

